{number: 72}
{title: Living for Jesus}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] Living for Jesus a life that is true,
Striving to [F] please Him in [C] all that I do;
Yielding al-[F] legiance, glad-hearted and [C] free,
This is the [D7] pathway of blessing for [G7] me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
O [C] Jesus, Lord and Savior, I give myself to Thee,
For [F] Thou, in Thine a-[G7] tonement, didst [C] give Thyself for me;
I [C] own no other Master, my [F] heart shall be Thy throne;
My [C] life I give, hence-[G7] forth to live, O Christ, for Thee a-[C] lone.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C] Living for Jesus Who died in my place,
Bearing on [F] Calv'ry my [C] sin and disgrace;
Such love con-[F] strains me to answer His [C] call,
Follow His [D7] leading and give Him my [G7] all.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[C] Living for Jesus through earth's little while,
My dearest [F] treasure, the [C] light of His smile;
Seeking the [F] lost ones He died to re-[C] deem,
Bringing the [D7] weary to find rest in [G7] Him.
{end_of_verse}
